  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF Catalytic funding to support the Education Services Joint Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catalytic funding to support the Education Services Joint Fund (ESJF). The ESJF is a critical aspect of the Ministry of Education, UNICEF and RNE partnership which directly contributes to the National Education Sector Investment Plan (NESIP) priority on improving governance and management. Through the Fiduciary Agent, UNICEF and RNE will contribute to MoE capacity building in financial management, procurement and programme implementation, key functions to deliver on the NESIP. The Fiduciary Agent and UNICEF complement each other in the provision of the necessary capacity required by the MoE, with the former focusing on finance and procurement and the latter on overall management and program implementation. The agreement further supports the Malawi government on inclusive education focusing on children with disabilities, improving opportunities for continuous professional development of teachers and evidence-based policy development.</narrative>
  </description>
